<p><img src="https://cdn3.brettterpstra.com/uploads/2026/09/gollygee-header-rb.7533.jpg" width="800" height="226" style="margin:0 auto;clear:both;" class="header" /></p>

<p>I already made <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/gollygee/id6809184721">GoLlyGee</a> for fun. Then I thought: what the heck, make a Mac version… also just for fun.</p>

<h3 id="same-toy-more-screens">Same toy, more screens</h3>

<p>See my <a href="https://brettterpstra.com//2026/09/09/just-for-fun-gollygee-game-of-life-visualization/">intro post from a couple of days ago</a> for the original announcement.</p>

<p>GoLlyGee is still Conway&rsquo;s Game of Life as a calm little visualization: colors, speed, liquid cells, ambient Watch mode, the whole tiny feature list. The Mac build is Mac Catalyst, so it is the same app family as the iPhone and iPad versions, not a separate rewrite with a separate price tag.</p>

<p>Resize the window and the board grows with it. Hit settings when you want softer blobs instead of square cells. Leave it running in a corner while you pretend to work. That&rsquo;s the product pitch.</p>

<h3 id="one-price-everywhere">One price, everywhere</h3>

<p>It is a universal app. One <strong>$0.99US</strong> purchase gets you iPhone, iPad, Mac, and the Apple Watch companion. I am not building a platform empire. I am selling a screensaver with opinions.</p>

<p>If you already grabbed it on iOS, the Mac version should come along with that same purchase once it is live on the Mac App Store side of the listing.</p>

<h3 id="one-more-thing-interactivity">One more thing: interactivity</h3>

<p>A short tap still brings up the little toolbar. Hold your finger (or mouse button) down and GoLlyGee drops a <strong>5×5 randomized patch</strong> of live cells onto the board — soup, not a solid brick, so it tends to keep thrashing instead of freezing into still lifes. Keep holding and drag to paint more of that chaos wherever you like.</p>

<p>It is a small change, but it turns the screensaver into something you can poke.</p>

